  "title": "A Systematic Comparison of TerraMind and THOR",
  "summary": "arXiv:2607.18504v1 Announce Type: cross\nThis study investigates how two Geospatial Foundation Models (GFMs), THOR and TerraMind, differ in design philosophies and performance across multiple use cases, highlighting architectural and use-case-specific factors.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The study benchmarks Geospatial Foundation Models (GFMs) and identifies architectural differences between THOR and TerraMind.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "THOR introduces a compute-adaptive architecture supporting variable patch sizes and unifies Sentinel-1, -2, and -3 data at native resolutions.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "TerraMind enables any-to-any cross-modal generation, leveraging a dual-scale token/pixel objective to infer missing sensors at inference time.",
      "confidence": 0.95
